- 'POs created before 2015' / 'purchase orders created since March 2024' -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with a 'created_before' or 'created_since' filter whose value is an ISO date 'YYYY-MM-DD'. A date bound satisfies the PurchaseOrder root requirement, so no PO id is needed. Use ONLY when the question names an ABSOLUTE date or year.
- RELATIVE OLDER: 'older than 6 months' / 'older than N months' / 'older than 1 year' / 'older than N years' / 'stale' / 'more than 6 months old' -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with an 'older_than_n_months' filter whose value is {"months": N} (convert years to months: 1 year -> 12, 2 years -> 24). Routes to the created_before tool arg; the planner computes the ISO cutoff from N. Do NOT compute the date yourself and do NOT emit 'created_before' directly.
- RELATIVE RECENT: 'in the last 6 months' / 'in the last N months' / 'in the last year' / 'from the last 12 months' / 'created in the last N months' / 'created within the past N months' -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with a 'created_in_last_n_months' filter whose value is {"months": N}. Routes to the created_since tool arg; the planner computes the ISO cutoff from N. Do NOT compute the date yourself and do NOT emit 'created_since' directly. The distinction from 'older_than_n_months' matters: 'last N months' means SINCE the cutoff; 'older than N months' means BEFORE it.
- LAST-UPDATED OLDER: 'not touched in the last N months' / 'not updated in the last year' / 'last modified N months ago' / 'no recent activity in the last N months' / 'no updates in the last N months' / any phrasing that names LAST MODIFIED / LAST UPDATED / LAST TOUCHED / LAST ACTIVITY / 'not touched' AND carries an explicit N -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with an 'updated_older_than_n_months' filter whose value is {"months": N}. Routes to the last_updated_before tool arg; the planner computes the ISO cutoff from N. Do NOT route to 'older_than_n_months' — that filters CreationDate, and answering a last-updated question with a creation-date cutoff answers a different question, silently and wrongly.
- LAST-UPDATED RECENT: 'POs updated in the last N months' / 'POs with activity in the last year' / 'recently updated POs in the last N months' -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with an 'updated_in_last_n_months' filter whose value is {"months": N}. Routes to the last_updated_after tool arg; the planner computes the ISO cutoff from N. The distinction from 'updated_older_than_n_months' matters: 'last N months' means SINCE the cutoff; 'not touched in N months' means BEFORE it. Do NOT route either to the CreationDate filters (older_than_n_months / created_in_last_n_months) — those filter a different column.
- VAGUE RECENT: 'recent purchase orders' / 'new purchase orders' / 'latest POs' / 'fresh POs' / 'the most recent POs' / 'recently created POs' — where the adjective names recency but gives NO explicit N — -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with a 'created_in_last_n_months' filter whose value is {"months": 3} (the default window). Do NOT set unanswerable=true for a vague recency adjective: the user is asking about recent POs, and refusing converts English into a SQL-shaped demand. The default fires only when NO explicit N is present; when the user says 'in the last 6 months', use months=6 as usual. Do NOT route to 'updated_in_last_n_months' — 'recent' here means recently CREATED, not recently modified.
